course: dictionary
lesson: 12329
title: Spotting fakes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A counterfeit thing is made to look exactly like something real, so that people will be tricked into believing it is real. «The shopkeeper held up the note. "This is counterfeit," she said.» Counterfeit means fake. The shopkeeper was not saying the note was cheap or old, but that someone had copied it to cheat people.
explain: Clues in the sentence help you work out the meaning. Words like "trick", "fake" and "illegal" show that counterfeit is about cheating. «Counterfeit trainers look real in the shop, but they fell apart after one week.» The trainers looked real, but they were not, so counterfeit must mean fake.
explain: Counterfeit can be a describing word, a naming word, or an action word. «Counterfeit money» describes the money. «The gang found a counterfeit» names a fake copy. «They were caught trying to counterfeit notes» uses it as an action word meaning to make fake copies.
fact: Counterfeit means made to look exactly like something real in order to trick people.
fact: «Counterfeit» can describe things, such as «counterfeit money» or «counterfeit goods».
fact: As a noun, «a counterfeit» means a fake copy of something real.
fact: As a verb, «to counterfeit» means to make fake money or goods illegally.
fact: Banknotes have special features, such as holograms and watermarks, to help people spot counterfeit notes.
exercise: «The shop took the note to the bank because it was counterfeit.» What does counterfeit mean? | Very old and valuable | Brand new and shiny | *Fake, made to trick people | Printed in a big city
exercise: «The police found a box of counterfeits in the warehouse.» What is a counterfeit here? | A safe box for money | *A fake copy | A police officer | A shop receipt
exercise: Nadia says counterfeit means real but cheap. Why is she wrong? | It is a kind of coin from long ago | It means cheap but real | *It means made to look like something real to trick people | It means very new
test: «Counterfeit trainers look real but fall apart in a week.» What does this tell you? | They are the oldest trainers ever made | They are real and well made | *They are fake, copied to trick people | They are the newest style in the shop
test: In «They were caught trying to counterfeit notes», what kind of word is counterfeit? | *An action word, meaning to make fake copies | A describing word | A naming word | A word for a colour
exam: Which sentence uses counterfeit as a describing word? | *The shopkeeper refused the counterfeit ten-pound note | The gang was arrested for counterfeiting | A counterfeit was found in the bin | They counterfeited the medicine for years
